/* TC002CLI/main.swift — hilfetext */
"cli.hilfe" = "mqtttc002 — send messages to an Ulanzi TC002.\n\nUses the setup of the Pixel Clock Messenger app: broker, password and clocks\nare read from there. Setting up happens in the app only.\n\nEvery clock is served on the way that is set for it in the app — HTTP or\nMQTT. \"mqtttc002 clocks\" shows which one.\n\nUSAGE\n  mqtttc002 [send] <text>          send text to the clocks\n  mqtttc002 message <text>         a one-time message over the loop\n  mqtttc002 dismiss [<name>]       take away the visible message,\n                                   or the named one\n  mqtttc002 delete <display>       remove a named display\n  mqtttc002 switch <display>       switch to a display\n  mqtttc002 image <name>           send a finished image from the stock\n  mqtttc002 layout <file.json>     send a layout (boxes with content) from a file\n  mqtttc002 screen                 read the clock's display and print it as text\n  mqtttc002 clocks                 list the clocks that are set up\n  mqtttc002 icons                  list the icons that are there\n  mqtttc002 images                 list the 16x52 images that are there\n  mqtttc002 effects                list the clock's effects, overlays and palettes\n  mqtttc002 display on|off         switch the panel on or off\n  mqtttc002 brightness <0-255>     the panel brightness (raw, not a percentage)\n  mqtttc002 moodlight ...          flood the panel with one color, or \"moodlight off\"\n  mqtttc002 indicator <1-3> ...    set one of the three indicators, or \"indicator <1-3> off\"\n  mqtttc002 next | previous        one display forward or back\n  mqtttc002 state                  print the clock's state\n  mqtttc002 settings               print the clock's settings by group\n  mqtttc002 settings set <key> <value>   change a setting\n  mqtttc002 tls                    the TLS state for MQTT (read only)\n  mqtttc002 tls ca <file.pem>      load the broker's CA onto the clock\n  mqtttc002 tls ca remove          remove the uploaded CA\n  mqtttc002 help                   this text\n\nAn image is a whole display (16x52) from the app's editor and replaces text\nand icon. Of the options below only --to, --name and --duration apply to it;\neverything else formats text, which an image has none of. A single frame\ngoes to the clock pixel-exact as a still, several as an animated GIF.\n\nA layout divides the full display into boxes, each with exactly one content (text,\nicon, chart, progress, drawing); the file carries exactly the keys of the device\nreference, either the \"layout\" block or the whole payload\n{\"layout\":{...},\"durationMs\":10000}. Of \"send\" the options --to, --name, --duration,\n--lifetime, --keep, --expiry and --dry-run apply. The TC001 cannot do layouts; the\ntool asks the clock about it and says so before sending. With --name the layout is\nstored under one of the slots (meldung1 to meldung5).\n\n\"screen\" reads the display over HTTP or MQTT (cmd/screen/get -> state/screen) and\ndraws it as text: one character per pixel, \".\" is black, \"#\" the first other color\nin reading order, then A, B, ...; below it the colors as #RRGGBB.\n\nCONTROLLING THE CLOCK\n  All these commands go to the clocks like \"send\" (--to, --dry-run); \"state\",\n  \"settings\" and \"tls\" only read. The tool never switches TLS on itself.\n  moodlight --color #RRGGBB | --kelvin 1000-40000 [--brightness 0-255]\n                      color or kelvin, not both; omitted values keep their value\n  indicator <1-3> --color #RRGGBB [--blink <ms>] [--fade <ms>]   0-65535 ms\n  settings set: the clock's keys such as \"volume\", \"clockFace\", \"transitionEffect\";\n                      sub-fields as \"scroll.speed\" or \"weekdayBar.show\"; yes/no as\n                      on/off. \"settings\" shows the keys. \"enlargeApps\" and everything\n                      of the system configuration (Wi-Fi, broker, firmware) is not set by\n                      the tool.\n  tls, tls ca: over HTTP only, the clock needs an address.\n\nOPTIONS FOR \"send\"\n  --to <clock>        name or address; may be given more than once.\n                      Without it, the selection that applies in the app.\n  --name <display>    name of the display on the clock (default: cli)\n  --color #RRGGBB     default: #00FF66\n  --icon <number>     an 8x8 icon to the left of the text\n  --font <name>       default: Silkscreen\n  --size <number>     default: 8\n  --bold              bold cut, if the font has one\n  --upper             everything in capitals\n  --top|--middle|--bottom       vertical alignment (default: middle)\n  --left|--center|--right       horizontal alignment (default: left)\n  --margin <number>   rows left free at top/bottom (default: 1)\n  --gap <number>      empty columns between the characters (default: 1)\n  --duration <seconds>  how long the clock shows the display\n  --lifetime <seconds>  after this time the display expires by itself (send only;\n                      default: 1800, i.e. 30 minutes)\n  --keep              the display does not expire, it stays until it is deleted\n  --expiry remove|mark  what then happens: delete it, or leave it standing\n                      with a red frame (default: remove)\n                      The lifetime is remembered with the slot.\n  --speed langsam|mittel|schnell   only for scrolling text\n  --dry-run           only show what would be sent\n\nLOOK (for \"send\" and \"message\")\n  The tool asks the clock for the names (\"mqtttc002 effects\" shows them) and\n  checks them before anything is sent. Text that the app rasters itself\n  (the default) covers the background completely: --background and --effect\n  do not work then, --overlay does.\n  --background #RRGGBB   solid background (not with --effect)\n  --effect <name>     moving background; --effect-speed <0.1-10>\n  --overlay <name>    weather over everything: rain, snow, drizzle, storm, thunder, frost\n  --palette <name>|#RRGGBB,#RRGGBB|#RRGGBB@0,#RRGGBB@100\n                      a name from the clock, 1-16 colors or colors with position 0-100\n  --palette-stepped   hard bands instead of a blend\n  --palette-span <pixels>, --palette-speed <0-10>   only for text from the palette\n  --text-palette      paint the clock's own text from the palette\n\nCHART AND PROGRESS (instead of text; for \"send\" and \"message\")\n  --bars 1,2,3 | --line 1,2,3   up to 16 whole numbers; a line needs two\n  --fixed-scale       fixed scale 0-8 instead of fitting itself\n  --chart-color #RRGGBB|palette\n  --progress <0-100>  bar in the bottom row\n  --progress-color #RRGGBB|palette, --progress-track #RRGGBB\n\nOPTIONS FOR \"message\"\n  Text and format as with \"send\"; --name here is the name of the message\n  (the only way to dismiss it later), --duration how long it stays.\n  Default: the message stays, wakes the panel and runs through twice.\n  --no-hold           stays only --duration long, not until dismissed\n  --no-wakeup         does not show when the panel is off\n  --replace           replaces the visible one instead of queueing behind it\n  --repeat <number>   how often scrolling text runs through (default: 2)\n\nOver MQTT the tool waits for the clock's answer (<topic>/result): if the clock\nrejects, code and field go to the error output and the call ends with 1. If no\nanswer comes there is only a warning — the same meaning as in the app.\n\nThe German names work as well: senden, nachricht, zurueckziehen,\nloeschen, umschalten, bild, uhren, bilder, effekte, bildschirm, hilfe, helligkeit, weiter, zurueck, zustand, einstellungen, setzen, entfernen, --blinken, --blenden, --an, --farbe, --schrift,\n--groesse, --fett, --gross, --oben, --mitte, --unten, --links, --zentriert,\n--rechts, --rand, --abstand, --dauer, --lebensdauer, --behalten, --ablauf (entfernen,\nmarkieren), --nicht-halten, --ersetzen, --nicht-wecken, --wiederholungen,\n--tempo, --trocken, --hintergrund, --effekt, --effekt-tempo, --palette-hart,\n--palette-spanne, --palette-tempo, --balken, --linie, --feste-skala,\n--diagrammfarbe, --fortschritt, --fortschrittsfarbe, --fortschrittsgrund.\n\nEXAMPLES\n  mqtttc002 \"Coffee ready\"\n  mqtttc002 send \"Mail is here\" --icon 1673 --color \"#FFAA00\"\n  mqtttc002 send Attention --to Kitchen --duration 10 --center\n  mqtttc002 image Heart --name meldung3\n  mqtttc002 send Weather --lifetime 600 --expiry mark\n  mqtttc002 send Permanent --keep\n  mqtttc002 send Rain --text-palette --palette Ocean --overlay rain\n  mqtttc002 send --line 3,5,2,8 --chart-color \"#00FF66\" --progress 40\n  mqtttc002 message \"Door open\" --name door\n  mqtttc002 dismiss door\n  mqtttc002 delete cli\n  mqtttc002 layout three-boxes.json --name meldung2 --dry-run\n  mqtttc002 screen --to Kitchen\n  mqtttc002 display off --to Kitchen\n  mqtttc002 moodlight --kelvin 2700 --brightness 80\n  mqtttc002 indicator 1 --color \"#FF0000\" --blink 500\n  mqtttc002 settings set volume 40\n\nTexts that are too long scroll by themselves; the app does the same.";

